  "source_path": "/scratch/ziv_baretto/Thesis_Ziv/Capstone-Thesis-/DATA_SET_BUILDER_AND_EXPLORER/Timeline_Maker/output_merged_v3/food_safety/Mehndi Hassan vs State Of U.P. on 3 October, 2023.json",
  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mehndi Hassan vs State Of U.P. on 3 October, 2023 Author: Samit Gopal Bench: Samit Gopal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2023:Ahc:189478 Court No. - 69 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 1865 of 2008 Revisionist :- Mehndi Hassan Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Revisionist :- Rajeev Sisodia,Ajay Kr Mishra,Atul Sisodia Counsel for Opposite Party :- Govt. Advocate Hon'ble Samit Gopal,J. 1.",
    "facts": "The present revision was admitted vide order dated 15.7.2008 and the revisionist was directed to be released on bail. The amount of fine was not stayed which was directed to be paid by the revisionist. 7. The facts of the case are that the complainant Ram Prakash, Food Inspector, Zoya stopped the revisionist on 14.12.1991 at about 09:45 a.m. while he was carrying about 80 kilograms of milk in 04 containers which was intended for sale. On suspicion of it being adulterated, he disclosed his identity to the accused and label, notice, receipt and code slip no. M.B.D.258 were prepared and asked the accused to give sample of the milk but the same was refused by him. The accused took the government papers from the complainant and tore them and took them away abusing him. The complainant then took sanction from the C.M.O. concerned and filed a complaint against the revisionist/accused. In the trial court the complainant/Ram Prakash was examined as P.W.-1, Pramod Kumar clerk was examined as P.W.-2, Om Prakash Sanitary Supervisor was examined as P.W.-3. The accused/revisionist in his statement under Section 313 Cr.P.C. denied the prosecution case and stated of false implication. No defense evidence was led. The appeal was preferred against the same which came to be dismissed after which the present revision has been filed against both the impugned judgement and orders. 8. The records show that Ram Prakash prepared a note of the spot of which Om Prakash/P.W.-2 is a witness, which is Ext.Ka-1 to the records, the F.I.R. being Ext. Ka-3 has also exhibited which has been lodged by Ram Prakash against the accused for the offence under Sections 186, 504 I.P.C. at Police Station Dehat Amroha, District Moradabad. The report of P.W.-1 Ram Prakash for lodging of the F.I.R. is Ext. Ka-2 to the records. The sanction to prosecute the accused/revisionist by the C.M.O. concerned has been accorded for the offences under Section 7/16 and 16(1)(C) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 whereas the complaint dated 21.12.1991 has been filed by P.W.-1 Ram Prakash for the offence under Section 16(1)(C) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. The place where the alleged incident is said to have taken place is a road described as Zoya Road, Chidiya Bagh, Amroha. Despite Mehndi Hassan vs State Of U.P. on 3 October, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/146211343/ 2 the same there is no independent witness to support the prosecution story.",
